  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Animation plays a vital role in this project. \nOne of the most aspiring
    goals is to create expressive animations that will support the dialogues as if
    the characters are really acting, instead of just interpolating between default
    clips. We want to get rid of simple text-readings, incorporate believable voice
    acting and breathe life to the characters as much as we can! Treat the game as
    if it's characters star in an animated movie, giving lots of small details for
    the player to discover about their life in Truffleton island, as a core aspect
    of the gameplay. \nWe wish to end up with a cartoon tale that will encourage:
    \n- Interaction with the local characters to learn more about their community
    and culture\n- Observation of their everyday lives and thoughts that can have
    an impact on how the narrative is perceived\n- Constant lookout and openess to
    be surprised\n\nAnimation will be the main source provider for all that.\n\nThat's
    why we have decided to use 2 different kinds of animation clips in the game for
    each character:\n1. Generic clips:\nUsed in the Animator controller to load default
    clips triggered by some actions (generic talk/walk/idle etc)\n2. Timeline clips:\nSpecific
    clips that will accompany certain dialogues/situations that reveal a lot about
    the characters personality and will only be loaded on specific occassions in
    the game."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fe129390af88b40faa85c89db6820ea6, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: -5592514773993622969, guid: fe129390af88b40faa85c89db6820ea6,
    type: 2}
