  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'We used narrative design to bring across some key points of the story
    and the whole theme to the players, that - together with the gameplay-  would
    result in a tailor-made and unique experience for everyone.


    Starting from
    the official guidelines  this project was declared to be an action-adventure
    game with a cooking theme, where the core  gameplay mechanics would be: exploration,
    talking with NPCs, small quests, and a bit of fighting and crafting (combining
    ingredients to create dishes).


    Having decided on the story to revolve around
    a cooking festival, the role of narrative in this experience resulted in a form
    of a puzzle where players would need to interact with the characters in order
    to figure out what the winning dish could be. So how was that achieved?'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fe129390af88b40faa85c89db6820ea6, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: -5592514773993622969, guid: fe129390af88b40faa85c89db6820ea6,
